# Design System Playbook — required reading

Before implementing, refactoring, or auditing any UI in `src/` for the PandaTrack redesign subproject, you MUST read:

**`docs/redesign/PLAYBOOK.md`**

The playbook contains accionable rules distilled from operational lessons of the redesign subproject. Each rule exists because something went wrong once. **Do not re-debate rules already in the playbook** — implement according to the playbook.

## What the playbook covers

1. **Component canonical sources** — when to use `<Button>` primary vs ghost vs destructive, when to use `<Modal>` vs `<Sheet>`, when `<Combobox>` vs `<MultiTagAutocomplete>`, etc.
2. **Token conventions** — `--border` vs `--border-strong`, `--text-on-accent` light vs dark, status enum tokens, layout magic numbers.
3. **Canonical patterns by scenario** — confirm modal destructive, autocomplete with tags, filter chips display, section card disabled-gated, field-as-attribute, toast neutral-undo.
4. **Anti-patterns explicit** — no `<select>` HTML native, no Portal+div modals, no hardcoded `text-white`, no hardcoded literals, no inventing variants without ADR.
5. **Mandatory workflow before implementing UI** — read playbook, demo HTML, component spec, ADRs, tokens.
6. **Self-audit checklist before closing** — TodoWrite, visual verification vs demo, comparative audit, validation, snippet-in-report.
7. **Cross-cutting handling during a session** — flag instead of silent fix.
8. **What to update when a module closes** — playbook, lessons-learned, cross-cutting registry, ADR.

## Related sources of truth

- `docs/redesign/methodology.md` — full methodology (phases, iteration, validation).
- `docs/redesign/_notes/lessons-learned.md` — historical journal of why each rule exists. Read for context, not for daily reference.
- `docs/redesign/_notes/cross-cutting-changes.md` — backlog of mini-corrective sessions (M0X / SN.X).
- `docs/redesign/components/` — per-component specs.
- `docs/redesign/decisions/` — accepted ADRs.
- `docs/redesign/tokens.md` — live token system.
- `docs/redesign/_notes/demo-screens.html` — visual source of truth (canonical anchors `#m01-vb-*` for modals; module anchors `#s6-*`, `#s7-*`, etc.).

## Reinforcing rules also `alwaysApply: true`

- `coding-standards.mdc` — base coding behavior.
- `english-code-only.mdc` — code in English, copy in i18n.
- `validation-checklist.mdc` — final validation commands.
- `theme-light-dark.mdc` — both themes are first-class.
- `modal-canonical-pattern.mdc` — Modal canonical component (this rule's sibling for Modal specifically).

## When this rule applies

- Any creation, refactor, or audit of UI components in `src/components/`.
- Any creation, refactor, or audit of pages in `src/app/`.
- Any work on the demo HTML in `docs/redesign/_notes/demo-screens.html`.
- Any audit of a screen against the demo.

## Skip if

- Pure data-layer / Prisma / server-action changes with zero UI touch.
- Pure documentation work in `docs/product/` (FRDs, etc.) without code consequences.
- Test infrastructure that does not render UI.

For everything else: read the playbook first.
